traceability.evidence:
Story: docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md

Core implementation:
- src/index.ts defines the ESLint plugin and is explicitly tagged to this story:
  /**
   * ESLint Traceability Plugin
   * @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
   * @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE - Provide foundational plugin export and registration
   * @req REQ-ERROR-HANDLING - Gracefully handles plugin loading errors and missing dependencies
   */
- Plugin structure and rule registry:
  - RULE_NAMES lists all rule module basenames:
    const RULE_NAMES = [
      "require-story-annotation",
      "require-req-annotation",
      "require-branch-annotation",
      "valid-annotation-format",
      "valid-story-reference",
      "valid-req-reference",
      "prefer-implements-annotation",
    ] as const;
  - Dynamic loading with graceful fallback on errors:
    const rules: Record = {} as any;
    RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => {
      try {
        const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
        rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
      } catch (error: any) {
        console.error(
          `[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
        );
        rules[name] = {
          meta: {
            type: "problem",
            docs: { description: `Failed to load rule '${name}'` },
            schema: [],
          },
          create(context: Rule.RuleContext) {
            return {
              Program(node: any) {
                context.report({
                  node,
                  message: `eslint-plugin-traceability: Error loading rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
                });
              },
            };
          },
        } as Rule.RuleModule;
      }
    });
  - Flat-config presets (ESLint v9 compatible) and plugin export:
    const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES = {
      "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
      "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
      "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
    } as const;

    function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
      return { rules: { ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES } };
    }

    const configs = {
      recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
      strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    };

    const plugin = { rules, configs, maintenance: { detectStaleAnnotations, updateAnnotationReferences, batchUpdateAnnotations, verifyAnnotations, generateMaintenanceReport } };
    export { rules, configs, maintenance };
    export default plugin;

Acceptance Criteria – Core Functionality & Rule Registry:
- tests/plugin-setup.test.ts (@story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP):
  it("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] plugin exports rules and configs", () => {
    expect(rules).toBeDefined();
    expect(configs).toBeDefined();
    expect(typeof rules).toBe("object");
    expect(typeof configs).toBe("object");
    expect(plugin.rules).toBe(rules);
    expect(plugin.configs).toBe(configs);
  });
- tests/plugin-default-export-and-configs.test.ts (@story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP):
  - Validates rule registry contents:
    it("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] rules object has correct rule names", () => {
      const expected = [
        "require-story-annotation",
        "require-req-annotation",
        "require-branch-annotation",
        "valid-annotation-format",
        "valid-story-reference",
        "valid-req-reference",
        "prefer-implements-annotation",
      ];
      const actual = Object.keys(rules);
      expect(actual).toEqual(expected);
    });
  - Validates configs.recommended and configs.strict (REQ-RULE-REGISTRY, REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM):
    it("[REQ-RULE-REGISTRY] configs.recommended contains correct rule configuration", () => {
      const recommendedRules = configs.recommended[0].rules;
      expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-story-annotation", "error");
      expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-req-annotation", "error");
      expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-branch-annotation", "error");
    });
    it("[REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM] configs.strict contains same rules as recommended", () => {
      const strictRules = configs.strict[0].rules;
      expect(strictRules).toEqual(configs.recommended[0].rules);
    });

Acceptance Criteria – Error Handling (already marked [x] in story):
- Implemented in src/index.ts via try/catch + console.error + placeholder rule.
- tests/plugin-setup-error.test.ts (@story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP):
  it("[REQ-ERROR-HANDLING] should report error loading rule and provide placeholder rule", () => {
    const plugin = require("../src/index");
    expect(console.error).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
      expect.stringContaining('Failed to load rule "require-branch-annotation": Test load error'),
    );
    const placeholderRule = plugin.rules["require-branch-annotation"];
    expect(placeholderRule).toBeDefined();
    expect(placeholderRule.meta.docs.description).toContain("Failed to load rule 'require-branch-annotation'");
    const fakeContext = { report: jest.fn() };
    const visitor = placeholderRule.create(fakeContext as any);
    visitor.Program({ type: "Program" });
    expect(fakeContext.report).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
      node: { type: "Program" },
      message: expect.stringContaining('Error loading rule "require-branch-annotation": Test load error'),
    });
  });
- tests/cli-error-handling.test.ts (@story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP) validates non-zero exit and helpful output when a rule is missing via ESLint CLI.

Acceptance Criteria – Integration with ESLint v9 flat config (REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT):
- The plugin exposes flat-config presets (configs.recommended and configs.strict) constructed from TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES.
- eslint.config.js uses ESLint v9 flat config format and wires in the plugin:
  - Loads plugin from ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js.
  - Adds it into flat config entries via:
    plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) }
- tests/config/flat-config-presets-integration.test.ts confirms the presets integrate correctly (recommended and strict presets enable traceability rules via documented usage).
- tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts (@story 001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP) executes ESLint v9 CLI with:
  const args = [
    "--no-config-lookup",
    "--config", configPath,
    "--stdin", "--stdin-filename", "foo.js",
    "--rule", "no-unused-vars:off",
    "--rule", rule,
  ];
  and verifies status codes for multiple cases (missing @story, present @story, missing @req, path traversal, absolute path), demonstrating working integration through flat config.

Acceptance Criteria – NPM packaging, TypeScript, and test setup:
- package.json:
  - name: "eslint-plugin-traceability" (standard ESLint plugin naming).
  - main: "lib/src/index.js"; types: "lib/src/index.d.ts".
  - files: ["lib", "README.md", "LICENSE", "SECURITY.md", "user-docs", "CHANGELOG.md"].
  - peerDependencies: { "eslint": "^9.0.0" } – explicitly targets ESLint v9.
  - devDependencies include TypeScript, @types/eslint, @typescript-eslint/utils, jest, ts-jest, etc.
  - scripts.test = "jest --ci --bail"; additional scripts for lint, type-check, etc., provide test infrastructure.
- tsconfig.json:
  - compilerOptions: { target: "ES2020", module: "CommonJS", declaration: true, outDir: "lib", strict: true, ... }.
  - include: ["src", "tests"].
- src and src/rules are all TypeScript files (*.ts), satisfying REQ-TYPESCRIPT.

Acceptance Criteria – Documentation & User Experience:
- README.md:
  - Installation:
    npm install --save-dev eslint-plugin-traceability
  - ESLint v9 flat config usage, e.g.:
    import js from "@eslint/js";
    import traceability from "eslint-plugin-traceability";

    export default [
      js.configs.recommended,
      { plugins: { traceability } },
      ...traceability.configs.recommended,
    ];
  - Quick start section showing how to create eslint.config.js, annotate code with @story/@req, and run ESLint.
  - Lists available rules and points to user-docs (eslint-9-setup-guide.md, api-reference.md, examples.md, migration-guide.md), which together document plugin structure and development/usage setup.
  - Documents how to run tests and quality checks.

